hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16030","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, he said, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ulathah narrated to us, he said, Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said, Khalid ibn al-Lajlaj narrated to us, that his father narrated to him, he said, while we were in the market, a woman carrying a boy passed, and the people rushed, and I rushed with them, and I reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was saying to her: Who is the father of this, and she was silent, and he said: Who is the father of this, and she was silent, and a youth beside her said, O Messenger of Allah, she is young in age, recent in covenant with jizyah, and she did not inform you, and I am his father, O Messenger of Allah. So he turned to those with him as if asking them about him, and they said, we know only good, or the like of that. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Are you married, he said: Yes. So he ordered him to be stoned, and we went and dug for him until we secured him, and we pelted him with stones until he became still, then we returned to our gatherings. And while we were thus, an old man was asking about the youth, so we stood to him and seized him by his collar and brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we said, O Messenger of Allah, this one came asking about the wicked one. He said: Hush, he is more fragrant with Allah in scent than musk. He said, so we went and helped him with his washing and his embalming and his shrouding, and we dug for him, and I do not know whether he mentioned the prayer or not."
